From 81cb14a4cae8493ea327f0f49029309830a01dc6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 10:00:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] filemanager: list and editor for touch screens, file
 operations
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The list was a table with fixed column widths in pixels (stored in
/etc/config/filemanager), on a phone it needed horizontal scrolling,
and the actions were small icons next to each other. Some operations
did not work as expected:

- names were put into the page as HTML (dom.append() uses innerHTML for
  a single string), a name with "<" or "&" was shown wrong or ran as
  markup; a name with "'" broke opening the file;
- cgi-upload answers 200 with {"failure": ...} when it cannot write,
  such an upload or save was reported as successful;
- saving a file opened through a symbolic link replaced the link with a
  regular file and set it to mode 777 (the mode of the link); saving
  any file made it owned by root; CRLF line ends and the BOM were lost;
- uploaded files got mode 0600 (cgi-io default), an existing file was
  replaced without a question;
- a FIFO was opened like a file; Duplicate and Delete of a large folder
  ended after the RPC timeout of the browser;
- the Save, Apply and Reset buttons were hidden by a rule for the whole
  page instead of not being created.

List:
- rows with flexible columns; on a narrow screen the size, date and
  permissions are shown under the name, the columns are hidden;
- ⋮ next to every item, a right click or a long press opens its
  actions: open, edit, hex editor, download, rename, properties,
  duplicate, copy, cut, copy path, delete;
- the path as buttons for every parent folder, a path can be typed
  (also of a file); folders first; sorting by a column or from a list
  on a phone; filter by name; the folder is in the address of the page,
  Back returns to the previous folder;
- several items can be selected to copy, cut, download or delete; Copy
  and Cut keep the items until Paste here in another folder; existing
  names are replaced or skipped after a question;
- uploads by the button or dropped files, with progress and cancel; a
  replaced file keeps its permissions and owner, new files get 0644;
- a file is downloaded with progress; a folder or several items as a
  .tar.gz made in /tmp (free space is checked); files larger than
  64 MiB are downloaded by the browser itself;
- properties: permissions as checkboxes or digits, owner and group,
  optionally for everything inside a folder.

Copy, move, delete of folders, archives and recursive changes run as
jobs detached from rpcd (setsid) in /tmp/luci-filemanager: the page
polls for the exit code and can stop the job; finished jobs are removed
after an hour.

Editor:
- a link is edited and saved through its target; permissions, owner,
  line ends and BOM stay as they were; a file changed on the router
  after it was opened is not overwritten without a question;
- line wrapping (on by default on narrow screens), line numbers, Tab
  inserts a tab, Ctrl+S saves; no autocorrection and capitals of the
  phone keyboard, 16 px font on touch screens; the editor fits the
  window; unsaved changes are kept when going back to the list and are
  asked about before they are lost;
- files that are not UTF-8 text open in the hex editor; files larger
  than 16 MiB are not loaded, larger than 2 MiB after a question.

Settings: start folder (last opened or fixed), folders first, columns
on wide screens, wrapping, line numbers, font size and height of the
editor. They are stored in /etc/config/filemanager as before; the old
column width and padding options are no longer used. The help is
translatable text; md.js and md_help.js are no longer loaded.

Checked in Chromium with luci-base 25.12, themes bootstrap and
proton2025, 1280 and 412 pixels wide, against rpcd file.* and cgi-io
from OpenWrt 25.12 with busybox: 47 checks each (CRLF, BOM, links,
owner and mode kept on save and upload, a change on the router before
saving, hex editor, create, rename, duplicate, copy and move with
conflicts and into itself, upload error, download of a file and of a
folder archive, chmod, recursive chown, delete, settings, the old
settings file, Back in the browser); no errors in the console.
